1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,049
(Supported by KOCCA)

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:03,789
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds are fictitious.)

3
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:05,090
(Children were filmed under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:52,270
Welcome...

5
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:56,340
Goodbye.

6
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:15,089
Welcome...

7
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:16,960
- You are here? - Yes.

8
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,530
Hey, hurry up and go. You will be late.

9
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:22,700
- Good work. - Did you get some sleep?

10
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:26,010
Do not even ask. My daughter was crying all night...

11
00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:27,340
because she missed her mom.

12
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:30,180
My wife was crying because she felt bad for our first child.

13
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,650
Man, I want to cry too.

14
00:01:32,910 --> 00:01:36,280
- When is she leaving the center? - She still has two days left.

15
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,620
But I am worried about when she comes back.

16
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,250
Hurry up and go. You will be late.

17
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,690
Okay.

18
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,760
Yes.

19
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,930
I finished the closing duties.

20
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:48,930
The spoonable yogurt does not sell well,

21
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,930
so I did not order any today.

22
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,470
Good job.

23
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,840
I am sorry for making you work the night shift on an important day.

24
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,170
If you are sorry...

25
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:03,040
This is my breakfast.

26
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:15,920
I am exhausted.

27
00:02:27,470 --> 00:02:28,870
(B202, 5 minutes)

28
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:30,870
Five minutes?

29
00:02:33,810 --> 00:02:35,640
(Do you want to look for a house together?)

30
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:36,940
(Onbang)

31
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:44,220
(Try it on!)

32
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:48,390
Thank you.

33
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:13,580
Boarding.

34
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:25,260
Sorry.

35
00:03:29,130 --> 00:03:30,500
("'I Didn't Know Back Then' Press Premiere D-Day")

36
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,800
("TV Star Tak Mu I, Can He Hit it Big on Screen?")

37
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,100
("Concerns Surrounding Him")

38
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:36,000
I have done plenty of press premieres for dramas.

39
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:40,370
Why am I so nervous?

40
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,170
Group blind dates and one-on-one blind dates...

41
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:44,310
are both nerve-racking.

42
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,650
Is that supposed to be a metaphor?

43
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:49,450
I am equally scared of reporters and women.

44
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,350
No matter what I say, they do not laugh or cry.

45
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:53,890
It is like they are betting on who can keep a straighter face.

46
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:57,260
I wonder why. You have so much charm,

47
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,160
so why are you not popular with women?

48
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:02,960
You act so well, so why do the reporters hate you?

49
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,600
Let us stop.

50
00:04:07,170 --> 00:04:08,670
The director changed halfway through,

51
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:10,170
and one actor dropped out due to school bullying.

52
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,370
But despite all that, the movie is still premiering.

53
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:16,410
- It has to. - Yes.

54
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:17,810
Let us go.

55
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:25,080
Are you nervous?

56
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:28,750
Yes, I am a little nervous.

57
00:04:28,850 --> 00:04:31,060
You won the Presidential Award at the Manhae Writing Contest.

58
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,120
(Everybody Dairy New Hire Interview)

59
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:33,830
Did you get into college with this?

60
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,160
Yes, I was admitted through special admission.

61
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,560
Why did you not continue writing?

62
00:04:38,730 --> 00:04:40,830
I felt like it was not my path.

63
00:04:40,930 --> 00:04:43,570
Oh, my. With this level of award history,

64
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:45,000
it is hard to say it is not your path.

65
00:04:46,070 --> 00:04:48,170
Your TOEIC score just passed the cutoff.

66
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:52,180
Zero internship experience. Zero study abroad experience.

67
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:53,950
Your GPA is 4.45.

68
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,780
I guess you only studied?

69
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:58,650
Yes, I really needed to get a scholarship,

70
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,090
so I worked hard.

71
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,890
And although I could not do an internship or study abroad,

72
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,290
I pride myself on having done every part-time job out there.

73
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:06,860
Essay tutoring, serving,

74
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:09,200
convenience stores, handing out flyers, call centers,

75
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:11,030
and even helping kids after school.

76
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,030
It seems you did not get any help from your parents.

77
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,100
To be exact, I did not accept any.

78
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:18,340
That is impressive.

79
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,609
Do you have a reason for applying to our company?

80
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:23,440
There were many other places considered dream jobs.

81
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:27,410
I liked the corporate mindset of Everybody Dairy...

82
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,750
where producers, workers, and consumers are all happy.

83
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:33,120
Also, since I was young, my mother told me...

84
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:36,590
that I grew up drinking this company's formula and milk.

85
00:05:36,690 --> 00:05:38,660
Since you raised me this much,

86
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:42,290
I wanted to be of help in growing the company now,

87
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:43,700
which is why I applied.

88
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:48,030
You applied for the HR department. Is there a reason?

89
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:50,400
I like people,

90
00:05:50,470 --> 00:05:52,670
and as the saying goes, HR is everything,

91
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:55,110
so I thought it might be the most important job.

92
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:57,080
That job requires you not to get too attached to people.

93
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:59,650
If you just hire me, I will work hard.

94
00:06:01,950 --> 00:06:04,320
- Thank you, everyone. - Thank you for your hard work.

95
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:05,920
Thank you for your time.

96
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,090
By the way, Ms. Gong Yu Il.

97
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:10,560
I really enjoyed reading your cover letter.

98
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:14,230
Oh, the story about the bamboo...

99
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:16,400
that does not break because it is hollow and has joints.

100
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:18,460
While everyone else is busy showing off...

101
00:06:18,530 --> 00:06:20,600
their strengths, skills, and experience,

102
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:24,640
you wrote about the pain, sadness, and frustration in your joints.

103
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,170
It was truly impressive.

104
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:30,110
You are confident you will not break, right?

105
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,910
Yes, thank you.

106
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,650
- It was a pleasure. - Good job.

107
00:06:33,710 --> 00:06:34,710
Good job.

108
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:04,940
No!

109
00:07:07,410 --> 00:07:08,610
No...

110
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,390
(Cast)

111
00:07:13,450 --> 00:07:14,790
(Ji Hoon, Tak Mu I)

112
00:07:14,850 --> 00:07:15,920
How was it?

113
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:20,290
(Cast)

114
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:22,290
It was boring.

115
00:07:42,950 --> 00:07:44,180
Is it raining there?

116
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,990
No, I am watering the plants.

117
00:07:47,450 --> 00:07:49,160
You are not watering them with your tears?

118
00:07:50,290 --> 00:07:53,930
I skipped watering for one day, and the soil is already so dry.

119
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:55,860
Tell me the truth.

120
00:07:55,930 --> 00:07:58,260
The money in your pockets is drying up too, right?

121
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,700
What?

122
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,640
What is this?

123
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:04,869
- Speak of the devil. - Yes.

124
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:06,410
How did you get here at this hour?

125
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:08,970
I had to meet your landlord for a location scout.

126
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,780
I went to check out a rooftop apartment for filming,

127
00:08:12,850 --> 00:08:15,580
and it was surrounded by buildings on three sides.

128
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:19,220
The landlord photoshopped the surroundings out...

129
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:22,090
and posted it online, and that runaway rookie...

130
00:08:22,150 --> 00:08:23,720
booked it without even visiting.

131
00:08:24,890 --> 00:08:26,590
Oh, my.

132
00:08:26,630 --> 00:08:29,730
The shoot is coming up soon. I thought I was going to get fired,

133
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,700
but then your place came to mind.

134
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:34,730
- So you want to shoot in my room? - No.

135
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:37,170
The room is a set, just the rooftop.

136
00:08:39,610 --> 00:08:41,740
What did the landlord say? Is it okay?

137
00:08:43,010 --> 00:08:45,380
They said it is fine as long as you agree.

138
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:48,080
They even offered to split the location fee half and half.

139
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,220
Then...

140
00:08:50,850 --> 00:08:54,190
- do I get paid too? - Of course you do.

141
00:08:54,550 --> 00:08:57,320
Even if we only shoot exterior, it will be completely chaotic.

142
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:00,760
- Then it is a deal. - Deal!

143
00:09:01,530 --> 00:09:04,960
- Right. Ryu Min is in your drama? - Yes.

144
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,830
Su Kyung will be thrilled.

145
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:10,000
She is going to annoy me so much.

146
00:09:11,070 --> 00:09:13,240
Hey, are you not going to your part-time job today?

147
00:09:14,410 --> 00:09:17,540
I am. I will go to the library and then work at night.

148
00:09:17,610 --> 00:09:19,180
You study at the library?

149
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:21,580
Why? What about the study cafe?

150
00:09:24,550 --> 00:09:26,220
Are you avoiding it because you went with that jerk?

151
00:09:26,250 --> 00:09:27,890
Because it breaks your heart?

152
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:32,120
No, it does not. I am going because it is free.

153
00:09:33,330 --> 00:09:36,660
They said they would open the library to graduates too,

154
00:09:36,730 --> 00:09:38,130
so I should take advantage of it.

155
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:41,400
And above all, going there makes me feel like I belong somewhere,

156
00:09:41,470 --> 00:09:43,370
so it puts my mind at ease.

157
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,640
Has that jerk Yong Seok contacted you?

158
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,680
The more I think about it, the angrier I get.

159
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:57,120
Hey. This fresh freshman...

160
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,950
met a pathetic returning student,

161
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,620
was a campus couple all through college,

162
00:10:00,690 --> 00:10:03,160
packed his lunches, wrote his reports,

163
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:05,120
and saved him a seat during every exam period.

164
00:10:05,190 --> 00:10:08,160
And then, as soon as he gets a job, "I have feelings for my coworker."

165
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:10,030
He just sends a text and ghosts you?

166
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:13,470
They say there are a lot of people like that.

167
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:14,999
People who fall in love at an orientation...

168
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,900
- for new employees. - Exactly.

169
00:10:16,970 --> 00:10:18,440
Hey, you should go to an orientation too.

170
00:10:19,610 --> 00:10:20,840
How did your interview go yesterday?

171
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:26,010
I have a good feeling about it this time.

172
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,880
That is great.

173
00:10:27,950 --> 00:10:30,220
Then are you coming when we meet the others tomorrow?

174
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:36,620
- I do not know. - Hey, we have to celebrate.

175
00:10:36,690 --> 00:10:38,960
If you do not show up at a time like this,

176
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:40,460
they will think you are jealous.

177
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:45,300
Well, I am a little jealous,

178
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:47,900
but, honestly, if I go, I am worried Su Kyung...

179
00:10:47,970 --> 00:10:50,170
will not be able to celebrate fully.

180
00:10:52,370 --> 00:10:53,870
Silly girl.

181
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,610
How can someone be so nice?

182
00:10:58,510 --> 00:10:59,850
Hey.

183
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:02,680
Eat a fresh one. Here.

184
00:11:14,730 --> 00:11:15,730
What is it?

185
00:11:17,230 --> 00:11:20,200
- Who is it? - Why invite us and fall asleep?

186
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:25,570
- Who did? - Who do you think?

187
00:11:26,970 --> 00:11:31,110
Da Hong lied. I knew something was weird.

188
00:11:31,210 --> 00:11:35,110
Now that you know, please leave. I am tired.

189
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:37,520
Because the press conference atmosphere was bad yesterday,

190
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:39,990
the director and all the staff had a team dinner,

191
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:42,820
and he stayed until the very end, so he barely slept.

192
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:46,190
He should have made an excuse and left early.

193
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:48,360
Is Mu I the type of person to do that?

194
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,500
Do you know what Mu I said yesterday?

195
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:51,900
"The staff worked so hard."

196
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:53,300
"I do not know when I will see them again."

197
00:11:53,370 --> 00:11:56,400
"Where would I go? My grandmother told me..."

198
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:57,470
"that no matter how good the set is,"

199
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:59,510
"and even if it seems like I will see those people again soon,"

200
00:11:59,570 --> 00:12:00,840
"I will not."

201
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:03,040
"She said to treat them well, as if every day is the last.'"

202
00:12:03,110 --> 00:12:04,540
"Two more over here."

203
00:12:06,410 --> 00:12:07,780
He is the only nice one.

204
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,920
So is he going straight into filming?

205
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:11,980
Without taking a break?

206
00:12:12,050 --> 00:12:14,290
The company is telling him to do that.

207
00:12:14,350 --> 00:12:16,890
But Da Hong said she would not do it unless it was with Mu I,

208
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:19,060
so CEO Ju came all the way to the set...

209
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,790
and begged him. Being soft-hearted is a disease.

210
00:12:23,130 --> 00:12:27,370
- Doctor, is this a disease too? - Yes, a serious one.

211
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,000
Then I should cure it.

212
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,710
Jae Gyu, when Da Hong arrives, go hang out somewhere else.

213
00:12:33,770 --> 00:12:35,070
I am really tired.

214
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:39,410
Da Hong suggested we meet here, so why is she not here?

215
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:43,720
You are getting prettier and prettier.

216
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:47,190
Right, just like that.

217
00:12:47,250 --> 00:12:49,460
Oh, my. Da Hong, you're here.

218
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,690
What is this?

219
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:55,660
She did not have a reservation,

220
00:12:55,730 --> 00:12:58,100
but she was in a hurry, so I took her first.

221
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,230
Hello.

222
00:12:59,970 --> 00:13:01,000
Get out.

223
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,039
- What? - You might not know...

224
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:05,470
since you just changed salons to follow me,

225
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:07,270
but this is my seat.

226
00:13:08,740 --> 00:13:11,410
Did you reserve it? Is your name written on it?

227
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,110
The lighting here is the prettiest.

228
00:13:13,510 --> 00:13:15,980
Hurry up and get out, okay? Get out!

229
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,520
Will you let go?

230
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:20,720
Oh, my. I understand.

231
00:13:20,790 --> 00:13:22,220
Oh, dear.

232
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:26,760
I am sorry, Min Ye. This is Da Hong's designated seat.

233
00:13:26,790 --> 00:13:28,860
It has been for a very long time.

234
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:30,330
I am sorry.

235
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:33,670
Oh, well...

236
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,669
We are almost done, right?

237
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:37,140
- Yes. - We still have the eyelashes...

238
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:39,640
It is fine. My eyelashes are naturally long anyway.

239
00:13:43,810 --> 00:13:45,910
Oh, my. I am sorry.

240
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:53,250
Oh, seriously. Why are you only like that to her?

241
00:13:53,350 --> 00:13:55,120
There is a reason for everything.

242
00:13:55,190 --> 00:13:57,190
Please make me look bright today.

243
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:59,730
On a depressing day, at least my face should look bright.

244
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,560
Who is so depressed?

245
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:03,200
There is someone.

246
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,700
Someone who is pretending to be fine,

247
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,200
but is actually terrified.

248
00:14:07,270 --> 00:14:08,470
You are making me depressed.

249
00:14:12,170 --> 00:14:15,310
"Is Tak Mu I only a star for television dramas?"

250
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,680
"Audiences who expected a romance line..."

251
00:14:17,740 --> 00:14:19,380
"will likely be completely disappointed."

252
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,520
"The movie, 'I Didn't Know Back Then.'"

253
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:26,320
"Tak Mu I looks like he is wearing clothes that do not fit."

254
00:14:26,390 --> 00:14:27,620
What are you doing?

255
00:14:27,690 --> 00:14:29,250
Are you a guy who reads malicious comments?

256
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,360
Hey, the director said...

257
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:34,090
he will edit it a bit before the release.

258
00:14:34,130 --> 00:14:35,290
Let's wait and see.

259
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,830
Editing what's already shot won't change much.

260
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:41,930
I really wasn't going to drink.

261
00:14:43,770 --> 00:14:45,970
Are you really going to do that project with Da Hong?

262
00:14:46,270 --> 00:14:49,110
She's headstrong, eccentric, and completely selfish.

263
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:51,340
What kind of rom-com can you do with a kid like her?

264
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,250
Will you even be able to get into character?

265
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,709
Why?

266
00:14:54,710 --> 00:14:56,480
When Da Hong and Mu I were in elementary school,

267
00:14:56,550 --> 00:14:58,420
they already shot a rom-com together.

268
00:14:58,880 --> 00:14:59,890
They did.

269
00:15:00,450 --> 00:15:01,690
I saw it with my own eyes.

270
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:09,390
Hey, Ju Da Hong's parents divorced because her mom cheated.

271
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:11,500
My mom said...

272
00:15:11,530 --> 00:15:13,300
she could even go to prison for adultery.

273
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:17,270
Min Ye, what's adultery?

274
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,970
I don't know. I heard Da Hong's dad...

275
00:15:20,010 --> 00:15:21,970
is even getting a test to see if she's really his daughter.

276
00:15:23,410 --> 00:15:24,680
How do they do that?

277
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:28,310
(Dressing Room A, Child Actors' Waiting Room)

278
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,250
It's okay. Don't cry.

279
00:15:33,690 --> 00:15:34,720
Okay?

280
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,560
Don't cry, Da Hong, it's okay.

281
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,530
(Yoon Jae Gyu, Age 11)

282
00:15:43,530 --> 00:15:45,660
Da Hong has been like that ever since,

283
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:49,130
saying Tak Mu I belongs to her and that she's going to marry him.

284
00:15:50,270 --> 00:15:51,870
I also didn't know Da Hong would stay...

285
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,710
so devoted for this long.

286
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:59,310
- Mu I, here comes your bride. - Here comes the bride.

287
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:02,010
Hey, you can't just barge into someone else's house.

288
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,750
That's the only way I get to see you guys.

289
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:05,680
Otherwise, you'd just say you're tired and not come out.

290
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:11,920
- Where's my drink? - Ju Da Hong.

291
00:16:11,990 --> 00:16:15,490
- Greet us first when you see us. - Oh, hi.

292
00:16:15,790 --> 00:16:18,000
What's this? Did you go to a salon?

293
00:16:18,930 --> 00:16:21,230
What are you talking about? I only put on some tone-up cream.

294
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,969
Where's the beer? My dark beer.

295
00:16:24,970 --> 00:16:27,210
Oh, all right. I'll go get it, just wait.

296
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:31,940
- Why should you go? I'll go. - Really?

297
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:33,450
Hurry back.

298
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:42,490
Welcome.

299
00:16:48,390 --> 00:16:51,660
Which one of these two is better?

300
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,800
Condoms?

301
00:16:54,730 --> 00:16:56,300
I'm asking...

302
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,500
which one is better between the two.

303
00:17:00,870 --> 00:17:01,870
Excuse me?

304
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:07,150
You must not be able to answer because you've never used them.

305
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,750
Then while we're at it,

306
00:17:10,850 --> 00:17:12,220
should we try them together?

307
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:17,220
- What? - Oh, my, what's with that look?

308
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:20,790
What are you thinking about right now?

309
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,100
I'm just saying there are a lot in the box,

310
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:25,330
so we should split them.

311
00:17:27,830 --> 00:17:29,740
- Excuse me. - What?

312
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,040
Honey?

313
00:17:34,670 --> 00:17:37,510
Young women these days are so open-minded.

314
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,180
You're making me blush.

315
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:46,390
Sir, your eyesight must be failing you.

316
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:49,690
It's all written right here. The left one is ultra-thin,

317
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:53,830
which means it's very thin. And it's strawberry flavored.

318
00:17:54,330 --> 00:17:56,700
The right one contains benzocaine,

319
00:17:57,130 --> 00:17:58,700
a numbing agent.

320
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,930
You know what that is, right?

321
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:02,100
Hey, you little brat.

322
00:18:02,870 --> 00:18:04,170
Are you looking down on me?

323
00:18:06,070 --> 00:18:09,110
- Sir, when did I ever... - Just because I'm bad at English...

324
00:18:09,170 --> 00:18:13,350
and failed the promotion exam, are you looking down on me too?

325
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:17,420
So what if a Korean is not good at English?

326
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:23,260
I am good at Japanese. I am really good at it, okay?

327
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:27,260
"How are you? Thank you for the food."

328
00:18:27,330 --> 00:18:28,330
How is that?

329
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:36,270
Why can you not answer? So you are looking down on me?

330
00:18:36,330 --> 00:18:39,570
Hey, you are just a part-timer. Are you looking down on me too?

331
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,640
You are looking down on me?

332
00:18:41,670 --> 00:18:42,940
You startled me!

333
00:18:43,010 --> 00:18:45,209
You startled me. What is it?

334
00:18:45,210 --> 00:18:48,910
I am sorry. I thought you were done. Please continue.

335
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,780
Hey.

336
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:54,420
Do you call that being good at Japanese?

337
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,020
Crazy jerk.

338
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,520
That is why you are a failure.

339
00:18:59,790 --> 00:19:01,990
Everyone probably knows you are a nuisance except you.

340
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:04,800
Guys like you are the most pathetic.

341
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:08,770
You get slapped somewhere else and cannot say a word about it,

342
00:19:09,230 --> 00:19:11,870
but you pick fights with people weaker than you.

343
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:13,740
"Excuse me."

344
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:17,680
Are you talking to me right now?

345
00:19:18,210 --> 00:19:19,810
No, my friend.

346
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:28,620
- I will call you back later. Bye. - You crazy idiot.

347
00:19:28,650 --> 00:19:31,560
You punk! Do you know who I am?

348
00:19:32,890 --> 00:19:33,890
I do.

349
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:38,930
A nuisance who is good at Japanese but bad at English.

350
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:42,270
- You punk! - Punk?

351
00:19:42,670 --> 00:19:47,010
- Who are you calling a punk? - Hold on.

352
00:19:48,810 --> 00:19:50,840
You seem very drunk,

353
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:52,680
and you must be under a lot of stress.

354
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:57,620
I will give you this. It is on me.

355
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:02,420
Drink it!

356
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,520
Gosh.

357
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:09,690
I drank it all.

358
00:20:13,470 --> 00:20:15,900
I will just take one of the ultra-thin ones.

359
00:20:15,970 --> 00:20:17,070
No.

360
00:20:17,770 --> 00:20:19,140
Keep the change.

361
00:20:39,290 --> 00:20:42,130
What? What is this? Did someone order this?

362
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,430
Gosh, awesome.

363
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:49,630
- Is it really good? - You are here?

364
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:51,670
- You are here? - Did you order food?

365
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:52,940
No.

366
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:55,239
What? Who is it from?

367
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,610
Who else? A fan must have left it.

368
00:21:00,810 --> 00:21:02,550
(Eat up and cheer up.)

369
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:04,120
"Eat up and cheer up."

370
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:06,250
See? It is a fan, right?

371
00:21:06,650 --> 00:21:08,650
Do not eat it. You do not know what is inside.

372
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:10,190
Gosh.

373
00:21:10,590 --> 00:21:12,259
How did they know my address?

374
00:21:12,260 --> 00:21:13,390
Are they a neighbor?

375
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:20,430
Da Hong.

376
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:23,700
What if someone made dirty jokes about you?

377
00:21:24,270 --> 00:21:27,140
- How would you feel? - Gosh, why would I let that slide?

378
00:21:27,170 --> 00:21:28,410
I would humiliate them.

379
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:30,710
Why?

380
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:32,310
Nothing.

381
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:35,480
Oh, right, I heard Ryu Min is going to be in your drama too.

382
00:21:36,110 --> 00:21:37,350
He is already doing so well as a singer.

383
00:21:37,420 --> 00:21:39,080
Why does he suddenly want to act?

384
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:41,850
I worked really hard to persuade him.

385
00:21:47,530 --> 00:21:49,460
- Let's go! - Okay.

386
00:21:57,070 --> 00:22:00,040
One, two, three, four.

387
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:04,440
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

388
00:22:04,510 --> 00:22:09,350
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

389
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:14,150
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

390
00:22:14,220 --> 00:22:19,160
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

391
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:26,500
Five, six, seven, eight.

392
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:30,070
One, two, three, four, five, six.

393
00:22:37,510 --> 00:22:39,110
"Be your name."

394
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:46,820
- All right, let's take a break. - Okay.

395
00:22:46,890 --> 00:22:47,890
- Great job, everyone. - Good work.

396
00:22:47,950 --> 00:22:49,350
- Great job. - Great job.

397
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:50,560
Let's go take a break.

398
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:03,230
I saw the articles.

399
00:23:03,970 --> 00:23:05,570
Should I call you an actor now?

400
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:10,140
Why are you being like this? It is not like that.

401
00:23:10,540 --> 00:23:11,680
Do your best.

402
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:16,920
("Rooftop Romance")

403
00:23:21,050 --> 00:23:22,290
(You have a new message.)

404
00:23:27,130 --> 00:23:30,760
(Thank you for applying to Everybody Dairy.)

405
00:23:30,830 --> 00:23:35,430
(We regret to inform you that we cannot offer you a position.)

406
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:48,880
- Boarding. - If they just told me like that,

407
00:23:48,950 --> 00:23:50,220
- wouldn't it be so nice? - Transfer.

408
00:23:51,650 --> 00:23:53,380
- Insufficient balance. - What?

409
00:23:53,790 --> 00:23:54,820
Darn it.

410
00:23:55,250 --> 00:23:57,860
- Insufficient balance. - "Insufficient memory."

411
00:24:01,090 --> 00:24:02,760
"Insufficient sleep."

412
00:24:03,190 --> 00:24:05,559
- Please hurry up. - I am sorry.

413
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:07,730
- "Insufficient patience." - Where is it?

414
00:24:11,070 --> 00:24:12,240
What exactly...

415
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:14,570
am I lacking?

416
00:24:18,010 --> 00:24:19,580
Sir, please wait a second!

417
00:24:22,450 --> 00:24:23,620
Thank you.

418
00:24:26,050 --> 00:24:28,250
"Insufficient common sense."

419
00:24:29,850 --> 00:24:31,520
(Research Corner)

420
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:48,670
("Successful Cover Letters")

421
00:25:02,750 --> 00:25:04,190
You are coming today, right?

422
00:25:04,420 --> 00:25:07,090
Even if you have to go to your part-time job, stop by for a bit.

423
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,930
(Yeon Ju)

424
00:25:09,330 --> 00:25:10,360
- Cheers! - Cheers!

425
00:25:10,430 --> 00:25:12,500
Bottoms up, or you are paying.

426
00:25:21,810 --> 00:25:23,510
I should have ordered an Earl Grey too.

427
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:24,810
This is too sour.

428
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:26,740
Hey, I told you not to use that word.

429
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:30,750
- Sorry. - "Sour."

430
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:33,380
Gosh, I need to be a designer so people will call me a pro.

431
00:25:33,450 --> 00:25:35,620
I am so sick to death of being called an assistant.

432
00:25:35,990 --> 00:25:38,660
Hey, do you guys have any idea how much hair splinters hurt?

433
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:41,130
When I go home, they are under my nails, in my clothes,

434
00:25:41,190 --> 00:25:42,530
and in my ears.

435
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:44,330
They get stuck everywhere and poke me,

436
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,030
and no matter how many I pull out, there are always more.

437
00:25:46,100 --> 00:25:48,099
Look, they keep coming out like zombies.

438
00:25:48,100 --> 00:25:52,300
- Our assistant goes through a lot. - Hey!

439
00:25:53,740 --> 00:25:54,740
Excuse me.

440
00:25:54,810 --> 00:25:57,810
- Four more Earl Greys, please. - Okay.

441
00:25:58,110 --> 00:25:59,740
It is driving me crazy too.

442
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:03,310
I finally got a junior after five years as a producer,

443
00:26:03,380 --> 00:26:07,520
and I was done being the youngest, but they quit after one month.

444
00:26:07,550 --> 00:26:09,220
- After I taught them everything. - What?

445
00:26:10,620 --> 00:26:12,090
Everyone is having a hard time.

446
00:26:12,820 --> 00:26:13,890
Lim Su Kyung.

447
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:17,000
In the midst of all this, congrats on joining a big company.

448
00:26:17,060 --> 00:26:20,130
Thank you. Good things come to those who wait.

449
00:26:21,500 --> 00:26:23,770
I thought everything would be great once I joined,

450
00:26:23,840 --> 00:26:26,240
but I am so stressed out because of my peers.

451
00:26:26,270 --> 00:26:28,910
- Why? - Is it because I am older?

452
00:26:28,970 --> 00:26:29,970
They only hang out among themselves.

453
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:31,480
I think they even have a separate group chat.

454
00:26:32,410 --> 00:26:35,050
- Is it really because of your age? - Hey.

455
00:26:36,610 --> 00:26:37,750
I heard you had an interview?

456
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:41,290
Yes, I failed.

457
00:26:44,790 --> 00:26:46,290
- See? - Gosh.

458
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:48,030
With that jerk Yong Seok and everything,

459
00:26:48,090 --> 00:26:49,760
why is nothing working out for you lately?

460
00:26:51,460 --> 00:26:54,030
You know, about your job hunt...

461
00:26:54,530 --> 00:26:57,040
When we park, there are spots if we go further down,

462
00:26:57,100 --> 00:26:59,440
but we circle because we do not want to go all the way down.

463
00:26:59,470 --> 00:27:02,770
Stop beating around the bush. What are you trying to say?

464
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,740
I was thinking you should lower your standards a bit.

465
00:27:04,810 --> 00:27:06,740
- We are getting older too. - Hey.

466
00:27:06,810 --> 00:27:08,110
Yes, that was a bit harsh.

467
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:09,679
Do you think she'd get that comparison...

468
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:11,380
- when she doesn't have a car? - What?

469
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:15,650
What? I am just upset for her.

470
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:18,689
I thought she'd make a living just by writing.

471
00:27:18,690 --> 00:27:19,920
When I was in second grade,

472
00:27:19,990 --> 00:27:21,090
I really do not remember anything else,

473
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:24,430
- but I remember her poem. - Yes, that one.

474
00:27:24,500 --> 00:27:28,330
- Titled "Spring Flowers." - Gosh, you have a good memory.

475
00:27:28,830 --> 00:27:31,670
Even the teachers said a genius had appeared.

476
00:27:31,740 --> 00:27:34,770
That poem was put up outside the staff room until we graduated.

477
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:37,080
Gosh, stop. That is all in the past.

478
00:27:37,140 --> 00:27:40,410
That's not all. She swept every writing contest there was.

479
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:41,950
Whenever she wrote a story, we would wait...

480
00:27:42,010 --> 00:27:43,050
to take turns reading it.

481
00:27:43,110 --> 00:27:44,520
Everyone said like father, like daughter...

482
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:48,020
How crazy! That is right. I went to the bookstore a while ago.

483
00:27:48,050 --> 00:27:52,090
Her father's new novel, is already a bestseller.

484
00:27:52,160 --> 00:27:53,690
I think he is so amazing.

485
00:27:53,760 --> 00:27:55,590
There must be some genetics involved in writing, for sure.

486
00:27:55,630 --> 00:27:58,260
Hey. I should get going.

487
00:27:58,330 --> 00:28:00,730
What? After only one drink?

488
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:03,970
It is time for my part-time job. I will pay for what we had so far.

489
00:28:04,040 --> 00:28:05,840
What are you talking about? I will pay.

490
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:08,240
No, you can treat me when you get your paycheck.

491
00:28:09,470 --> 00:28:10,980
- I am leaving. - Bye.

492
00:28:11,040 --> 00:28:13,580
Excuse me, I would like to pay.

493
00:28:14,280 --> 00:28:15,880
Hurry up and go.

494
00:28:15,950 --> 00:28:17,850
Here are your four Earl Greys.

495
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:18,920
Thank you.

496
00:28:23,420 --> 00:28:24,490
Hey.

497
00:28:25,220 --> 00:28:26,590
- What? - What? What is it?

498
00:28:26,660 --> 00:28:29,160
Gosh, you selfish jerks.

499
00:28:29,230 --> 00:28:31,500
- What did we do? - What?

500
00:28:32,100 --> 00:28:34,200
What about the parking lot?

501
00:28:34,270 --> 00:28:37,569
What are you saying to someone who has nowhere lower to go?

502
00:28:37,570 --> 00:28:39,870
Hey, Yu Il...

503
00:28:39,940 --> 00:28:42,010
has better grades than you, Su Kyung,

504
00:28:42,070 --> 00:28:45,610
and a better educational background. And she is prettier too.

505
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:48,710
Why tell her to lower standards when you will not lower yours?

506
00:28:48,780 --> 00:28:52,780
- Well, that's because... - And who wrote your cover letters?

507
00:28:53,280 --> 00:28:55,820
Who wrote your love letters?

508
00:28:55,890 --> 00:28:58,190
You guys really are ungrateful.

509
00:28:58,590 --> 00:29:00,490
I told you not to talk about her dad.

510
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:03,260
- Why do you keep bringing it up? - So why is she acting like this?

511
00:29:03,330 --> 00:29:05,200
You will not tell us anything, so we keep...

512
00:29:05,260 --> 00:29:10,330
I mean, just do not do it. She said she hates it, okay?

513
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:12,640
Why do you keep bringing up things she hates?

514
00:29:12,670 --> 00:29:14,409
That is why you get called an assistant,

515
00:29:14,410 --> 00:29:16,169
and you are always left out.

516
00:29:16,170 --> 00:29:17,640
- Hey! - What?

517
00:29:19,380 --> 00:29:20,950
Instead of wasting time drinking with you guys,

518
00:29:21,010 --> 00:29:22,980
I am just going to get some sleep.

519
00:29:23,050 --> 00:29:24,950
- Why, you little... - Seriously.

520
00:29:25,120 --> 00:29:26,120
Assistant.

521
00:29:51,910 --> 00:29:53,440
(The End)

522
00:29:54,380 --> 00:29:55,750
Done!

523
00:29:56,410 --> 00:29:57,850
Dad, I finished writing it.

524
00:29:59,550 --> 00:30:00,550
Right.

525
00:30:05,960 --> 00:30:07,690
You did a great job.

526
00:30:07,830 --> 00:30:10,760
Publishers will go crazy wanting to make this a children's book too.

527
00:30:10,830 --> 00:30:12,230
No, let us just keep it to ourselves.

528
00:30:14,370 --> 00:30:15,500
Okay.

529
00:30:15,570 --> 00:30:17,200
Well, if the author says so, we have to.

530
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,510
Dad, what kind of drawing would look good here?

531
00:30:24,310 --> 00:30:26,540
- A bear? - Yes.

532
00:30:30,780 --> 00:30:32,220
You need some sugar. Eat this while you write.

533
00:30:34,590 --> 00:30:36,550
Someone went abroad again?

534
00:30:36,620 --> 00:30:37,790
Yes, a junior colleague.

535
00:30:38,390 --> 00:30:40,160
They asked if I needed anything,

536
00:30:40,190 --> 00:30:41,390
so I just told them to bring back some candy.

537
00:30:42,830 --> 00:30:45,130
I do not know why they do not sell this candy here.

538
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:48,300
Is your work going well?

539
00:30:48,370 --> 00:30:50,600
Yes, I am right at the deadline.

540
00:30:50,670 --> 00:30:53,870
Goodness, you are going to be more famous than me.

541
00:30:53,940 --> 00:30:56,869
Well, you had better step it up, Dad.

542
00:30:56,870 --> 00:30:57,880
I will.

543
00:30:58,740 --> 00:30:59,740
Where is your mom?

544
00:31:00,950 --> 00:31:02,550
Mom?

545
00:31:02,610 --> 00:31:04,980
She is sleeping. She said she has a headache.

546
00:31:07,190 --> 00:31:08,190
Is that so?

547
00:31:09,490 --> 00:31:11,020
Dad.

548
00:31:11,090 --> 00:31:12,520
Mom keeps crying.

549
00:31:13,460 --> 00:31:14,460
Did you two fight?

550
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:17,360
Of course not.

551
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:20,870
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 2)

552
00:31:20,970 --> 00:31:22,030
I enjoyed reading it.

553
00:31:22,530 --> 00:31:24,370
You wrote it even better than Volume One.

554
00:31:24,440 --> 00:31:25,800
The ending is great too.

555
00:31:25,870 --> 00:31:26,870
Really?

556
00:31:26,940 --> 00:31:28,040
(Private Counseling Room)

557
00:31:28,170 --> 00:31:31,140
I think your writing...

558
00:31:31,210 --> 00:31:32,940
is really good.

559
00:31:34,710 --> 00:31:36,280
Well, I do not have anything else to give you.

560
00:31:38,920 --> 00:31:39,920
Have this.

561
00:31:40,890 --> 00:31:41,920
Wait.

562
00:31:43,390 --> 00:31:45,320
I actually brought some to give to you too.

563
00:31:47,830 --> 00:31:49,830
Oh, you did.

564
00:31:50,260 --> 00:31:51,900
But they do not really sell these in Korea.

565
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:53,360
How fascinating.

566
00:31:54,500 --> 00:31:55,500
I know, right?

567
00:32:03,110 --> 00:32:04,110
Mom.

568
00:32:05,810 --> 00:32:08,650
Mom, what is wrong? Why are you crying?

569
00:32:08,710 --> 00:32:09,710
What is all this?

570
00:32:11,080 --> 00:32:12,580
- What is this? - Your dad...

571
00:32:13,480 --> 00:32:15,990
Your dad says he wants to live with this woman.

572
00:32:17,490 --> 00:32:18,490
Woman?

573
00:32:29,570 --> 00:32:31,700
Oh, that cannot be true.

574
00:32:32,900 --> 00:32:34,510
He is not that kind of person.

575
00:32:52,260 --> 00:32:54,430
(Hometown Diner)

576
00:33:08,210 --> 00:33:09,940
Where is your mind wandering off to?

577
00:33:11,040 --> 00:33:12,040
Hello?

578
00:33:13,080 --> 00:33:16,850
Oh, I am just feeling sleepy,

579
00:33:16,910 --> 00:33:18,820
and bad thoughts keep coming to mind.

580
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:21,790
The thing about thoughts is,

581
00:33:21,850 --> 00:33:24,790
the good ones all run away somewhere,

582
00:33:24,890 --> 00:33:28,360
and the bad ones keep crawling in and rattling you.

583
00:33:29,790 --> 00:33:31,700
Does that happen to you too?

584
00:33:32,030 --> 00:33:33,960
Do you know what the good thing about getting old is?

585
00:33:34,330 --> 00:33:37,200
There were definitely more bad times,

586
00:33:37,270 --> 00:33:40,040
but miraculously, I only remember the good ones.

587
00:33:41,740 --> 00:33:46,580
My awful husband, my burdensome children,

588
00:33:46,610 --> 00:33:49,410
and my resentful parents are all gone,

589
00:33:49,850 --> 00:33:52,280
and everything is like a blooming April.

590
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:56,890
All the freezing and sweating is completely forgotten.

591
00:33:58,890 --> 00:33:59,890
Really?

592
00:34:00,660 --> 00:34:03,230
Does that make you want to grow old quickly?

593
00:34:04,430 --> 00:34:05,700
Hurry up and eat.

594
00:34:05,730 --> 00:34:07,870
- Yes, thank you for the food. - Okay.

595
00:34:31,990 --> 00:34:32,990
You startled me.

596
00:34:36,030 --> 00:34:40,430
Hey, what are you doing here? And what is all this?

597
00:34:41,900 --> 00:34:45,899
Ta-da. Our Ryu Min merchandise.

598
00:34:45,900 --> 00:34:47,970
I heard the news from Yeon Ju.

599
00:34:48,010 --> 00:34:51,080
If we display all of this in your room,

600
00:34:51,140 --> 00:34:53,140
Ryu Min will see it while filming.

601
00:34:53,810 --> 00:34:55,580
Imagine how encouraged he will feel.

602
00:34:56,650 --> 00:34:58,320
Did you come all the way here just for this?

603
00:34:58,380 --> 00:34:59,420
What about your work?

604
00:35:00,580 --> 00:35:01,720
Today is Sunday.

605
00:35:03,350 --> 00:35:04,360
Right.

606
00:35:08,090 --> 00:35:10,130
Yu Il, I am sorry about yesterday.

607
00:35:12,460 --> 00:35:15,470
I really only left because it was time for my shift.

608
00:35:15,500 --> 00:35:19,500
Right? I knew it. Yeon Ju was just overreacting.

609
00:35:22,940 --> 00:35:25,879
Well, this rooftop has a similar vibe to the original story.

610
00:35:25,880 --> 00:35:27,550
The wooden bench is nice, we can take down the clothesline,

611
00:35:27,610 --> 00:35:28,910
hang some lights here,

612
00:35:28,980 --> 00:35:30,920
and just move those things to the back, right?

613
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:38,390
"When does the filming end?"

614
00:35:38,460 --> 00:35:39,660
"Take some pictures and send them to me."

615
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:42,530
"If our Ryu Min needs to go, open up your bathroom for him."

616
00:35:42,590 --> 00:35:43,660
"Make sure you clean it."

617
00:35:43,730 --> 00:35:45,800
Su Kyung has been making a fuss since this morning.

618
00:35:45,860 --> 00:35:49,370
- You should not have told her. - I am regretting it now.

619
00:35:51,140 --> 00:35:52,640
- Hey, by the way, - Yes.

620
00:35:52,700 --> 00:35:54,540
seeing Ryu Min in person,

621
00:35:54,640 --> 00:35:58,310
- he really is handsome. - Yes, but do not tell her that.

622
00:35:58,380 --> 00:36:00,780
She gets upset because he does not look as good on screen.

623
00:36:00,810 --> 00:36:03,150
Then what should I say? That he looks better on television?

624
00:36:03,210 --> 00:36:05,980
No. Do not say anything at all.

625
00:36:06,050 --> 00:36:08,120
Just look at him.

626
00:36:08,790 --> 00:36:09,820
Who are you?

627
00:36:11,790 --> 00:36:12,820
Are you her friend?

628
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:15,630
- Hello. - Oh, hello.

629
00:36:15,690 --> 00:36:16,890
- Hello. - Hello.

630
00:36:18,260 --> 00:36:19,300
What? Con...

631
00:36:21,100 --> 00:36:22,100
Con?

632
00:36:25,970 --> 00:36:27,340
I want to eat corn cheese.

633
00:36:30,110 --> 00:36:31,140
Do you like corn cheese?

634
00:36:32,810 --> 00:36:34,950
Oh, yes, I guess.

635
00:36:35,450 --> 00:36:36,480
You like it?

636
00:36:38,350 --> 00:36:39,380
Well, then.

637
00:36:42,220 --> 00:36:43,790
Why is the convenience store worker here?

638
00:36:45,060 --> 00:36:46,320
Is she a staff member?

639
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:49,790
He did not have that kind of image when I saw him on television.

640
00:36:50,190 --> 00:36:51,930
He is not usually like that.

641
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:53,800
Does he like corn cheese?

642
00:36:55,470 --> 00:36:56,870
- See you. - Okay.

643
00:36:59,170 --> 00:37:01,870
I am usually the first one, but I lost my spot today.

644
00:37:01,970 --> 00:37:04,680
- I was worried. - Oh, there is no need to worry.

645
00:37:04,740 --> 00:37:06,140
You did perfectly fine at the reading.

646
00:37:08,050 --> 00:37:09,910
But Mu I, do you want to eat corn cheese?

647
00:37:12,020 --> 00:37:14,080
Oh, no, it is fattening.

648
00:37:15,120 --> 00:37:17,290
(Central Library)

649
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:21,390
(Gender: Female)

650
00:37:21,460 --> 00:37:22,730
(Save changes)

651
00:37:22,790 --> 00:37:25,530
(228 dollars)

652
00:37:26,460 --> 00:37:28,700
Why is the application fee 228 dollars?

653
00:37:29,900 --> 00:37:32,100
They are bleeding me dry.

654
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:38,140
Filming is done. Restoration is done.

655
00:37:38,210 --> 00:37:39,480
(Yeon Ju)

656
00:37:39,580 --> 00:37:40,580
Okay.

657
00:37:41,580 --> 00:37:42,780
(Okay.)

658
00:37:44,150 --> 00:37:45,150
Gosh.

659
00:37:56,590 --> 00:37:57,630
What is this?

660
00:38:00,130 --> 00:38:01,870
What is it?

661
00:38:04,470 --> 00:38:07,400
"I can hear everything even if you do not speak so loudly."

662
00:38:07,440 --> 00:38:08,670
What is this?

663
00:38:11,140 --> 00:38:12,310
(I can hear everything even if you do not speak so loudly.)

664
00:38:15,180 --> 00:38:16,280
It's still warm.

665
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:20,080
What is it?

666
00:38:21,820 --> 00:38:23,250
It's hot! Oh, gosh.

667
00:38:23,320 --> 00:38:24,320
Goodness.

668
00:38:35,470 --> 00:38:37,700
Hey, look at this.

669
00:38:38,040 --> 00:38:40,140
They know exactly where the cameras are.

670
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:42,570
Let us report this. We have to.

671
00:38:42,670 --> 00:38:44,710
Oh, they will not catch them even if we report it.

672
00:38:44,740 --> 00:38:46,440
We do not even know if it is a man or a woman.

673
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:48,780
And they did not even enter the house.

674
00:38:49,150 --> 00:38:51,650
Who would do anything for something like this?

675
00:38:51,980 --> 00:38:53,780
It will just be annoying going back and forth.

676
00:38:53,820 --> 00:38:56,050
The corn cheese was warm earlier.

677
00:38:56,650 --> 00:38:57,820
Is that not really creepy?

678
00:38:57,890 --> 00:39:00,160
It means they knew when you would arrive.

679
00:39:00,260 --> 00:39:01,330
Wait!

680
00:39:02,090 --> 00:39:04,760
You do not think they put drugs in the food, do you?

681
00:39:06,860 --> 00:39:08,030
They might have.

682
00:39:09,400 --> 00:39:10,830
Could it be someone around you?

683
00:39:11,370 --> 00:39:13,000
To just call them a fan,

684
00:39:13,070 --> 00:39:14,670
they know your house and your schedule.

685
00:39:16,610 --> 00:39:17,780
Someone around me?

686
00:39:19,740 --> 00:39:21,050
Oh, it is probably a fan.

687
00:39:27,320 --> 00:39:28,920
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 2)

688
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:32,060
You brought out the Buddhist scriptures again.

689
00:39:33,820 --> 00:39:36,930
Oh, I mean my mom, Mrs. Chu,

690
00:39:36,990 --> 00:39:39,100
recites Buddhist scriptures when she is anxious.

691
00:39:42,330 --> 00:39:44,900
I just want to get some sleep, forget about the movie.

692
00:39:47,470 --> 00:39:49,640
About this book, though.

693
00:39:49,710 --> 00:39:52,710
When is Volume Three coming out anyway? Seriously.

694
00:39:52,780 --> 00:39:53,780
This is really something.

695
00:39:55,010 --> 00:39:57,010
Tell me about it.

696
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:58,520
How many years has it been already?

697
00:40:01,050 --> 00:40:02,420
Did the author die?

698
00:40:02,490 --> 00:40:04,289
- Yeong Su! - Gosh.

699
00:40:04,290 --> 00:40:06,290
- What? - Oh, seriously.

700
00:40:08,660 --> 00:40:10,090
Oh, sorry, I almost cursed.

701
00:40:11,030 --> 00:40:12,260
You basically did.

702
00:40:12,330 --> 00:40:14,870
Look at your eyes. They are cursing me out.

703
00:40:17,900 --> 00:40:19,700
Oh, my, I can see him really well.

704
00:40:19,770 --> 00:40:21,510
- He is coming out. - He is handsome.

705
00:40:25,240 --> 00:40:27,280
Is Ryu Min not here yet?

706
00:40:31,820 --> 00:40:32,820
The convenience store worker?

707
00:40:33,850 --> 00:40:35,120
So she is not a staff member.

708
00:40:36,450 --> 00:40:37,590
Did she come to watch?

709
00:40:38,060 --> 00:40:40,590
No way. I think I just made eye contact with Tak Mu I.

710
00:40:40,660 --> 00:40:42,490
Are you crazy? It was me.

711
00:40:42,560 --> 00:40:43,660
He is so handsome, seriously.

712
00:40:45,100 --> 00:40:46,500
Hey, girls,

713
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:50,230
we are just faces in the crowd to him.

714
00:40:58,310 --> 00:41:01,450
Excuse me. You cannot take pictures.

715
00:41:09,890 --> 00:41:11,050
I was not taking a picture...

716
00:41:11,120 --> 00:41:14,790
The corn cheese story that only the people on set heard...

717
00:41:15,030 --> 00:41:16,030
I did not take any.

718
00:41:18,360 --> 00:41:19,830
And the black hoodie...

719
00:41:23,130 --> 00:41:25,600
Condoms to corn cheese?

720
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:28,240
All right, let's run the rehearsal.

721
00:41:28,310 --> 00:41:29,540
Let's run the rehearsal!

722
00:41:30,570 --> 00:41:33,180
- This is how they actually film it. - Please step aside.

723
00:41:34,980 --> 00:41:36,880
Check it first.

724
00:41:36,950 --> 00:41:38,750
- Check it first. - Yes, sir.

725
00:41:40,820 --> 00:41:43,420
Hello. Yes, where are you right now?

726
00:41:46,460 --> 00:41:47,690
This is bad.

727
00:41:49,160 --> 00:41:51,930
I keep seeing handsome celebrities lately,

728
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:55,230
so all the customers look...

729
00:42:14,250 --> 00:42:15,250
Are you going to ring me up?

730
00:42:19,260 --> 00:42:20,990
I said, are you going to ring me up?

731
00:42:22,060 --> 00:42:23,590
Oh, yes, I am sorry.

732
00:42:25,600 --> 00:42:27,800
(Roasted Squid)

733
00:42:33,870 --> 00:42:34,870
What?

734
00:42:35,870 --> 00:42:38,140
Well, he seems to have a good personality.

735
00:42:40,210 --> 00:42:42,080
I guess he likes corn cheese.

736
00:42:42,150 --> 00:42:44,620
Oh, my, that is quite modest for a top star.

737
00:42:47,080 --> 00:42:49,689
Honey, do you want to come home for dinner today?

738
00:42:49,690 --> 00:42:51,360
I made a lot of delicious food.

739
00:42:52,960 --> 00:42:54,290
What did you make?

740
00:42:54,360 --> 00:42:56,460
Your dad's favorite meat dish.

741
00:42:56,790 --> 00:42:58,600
Soup, fried food.

742
00:42:59,630 --> 00:43:02,370
Honey, have you ever heard of blowfish bulgogi?

743
00:43:02,430 --> 00:43:04,870
I learned a new recipe and tried making it.

744
00:43:05,200 --> 00:43:06,570
Is he coming?

745
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:08,070
He said he'd come weeks ago and didn't show up,

746
00:43:08,140 --> 00:43:10,370
so you had a hard time finishing all the leftovers.

747
00:43:10,910 --> 00:43:12,040
Oh, he said he is coming.

748
00:43:12,110 --> 00:43:14,110
He said he is definitely coming today.

749
00:43:14,440 --> 00:43:16,080
Oh, and you believe that?

750
00:43:16,110 --> 00:43:17,280
Do you really believe him?

751
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:20,980
Look, he is here.

752
00:43:21,050 --> 00:43:22,390
I told you he was definitely coming today.

753
00:43:22,420 --> 00:43:23,450
I have to go.

754
00:43:28,660 --> 00:43:29,730
Hello?

755
00:43:30,330 --> 00:43:31,360
Hello?

756
00:43:34,330 --> 00:43:35,600
Oh, welcome.

757
00:43:39,940 --> 00:43:40,970
What?

758
00:43:43,510 --> 00:43:45,410
Should I test the waters?

759
00:43:45,480 --> 00:43:46,980
Excuse me.

760
00:43:47,040 --> 00:43:49,910
I was actually wondering when you would come by.

761
00:43:50,480 --> 00:43:51,850
What? Did she recognize me?

762
00:43:56,950 --> 00:43:58,020
Retreat for now.

763
00:44:09,700 --> 00:44:10,700
(Roasted Eggs)

764
00:44:14,570 --> 00:44:16,010
That will be 1.8 dollars.

765
00:44:17,370 --> 00:44:20,710
The delivery truck will come by again later around 4pm.

766
00:44:20,780 --> 00:44:23,550
You can buy a salad lunchbox if you come back then.

767
00:44:24,580 --> 00:44:25,580
Okay.

768
00:44:27,020 --> 00:44:29,720
I just noticed you buy them often.

769
00:44:30,290 --> 00:44:31,390
And...

770
00:44:32,660 --> 00:44:35,760
thank you for last time.

771
00:44:36,030 --> 00:44:37,830
I realized I never got to say that.

772
00:44:46,170 --> 00:44:48,670
Oh, do you need anything else...

773
00:44:50,110 --> 00:44:51,170
Oh, no.

774
00:44:53,410 --> 00:44:55,250
What is his deal? Making me feel awkward.

775
00:44:59,850 --> 00:45:01,350
What? Did she not recognize me?

776
00:45:03,690 --> 00:45:04,720
No.

777
00:45:05,820 --> 00:45:07,520
She definitely recognized me as the condom guy.

778
00:45:25,310 --> 00:45:28,980
(Chaewoon Salad, I set it aside before it ran out.)

779
00:45:33,650 --> 00:45:34,890
Welcome.

780
00:45:40,120 --> 00:45:41,560
Are you looking for anything in particular?

781
00:45:41,630 --> 00:45:45,400
Oh, the woman who was working here just a moment ago...

782
00:45:45,430 --> 00:45:47,430
Oh, she just got off work.

783
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:48,970
Excuse me?

784
00:45:55,770 --> 00:45:59,440
- Your dad says he misses you. - Forget it. I do not want to hear.

785
00:46:00,480 --> 00:46:02,010
Your dad...

786
00:46:02,110 --> 00:46:03,580
asked his publishing company...

787
00:46:03,650 --> 00:46:07,350
Mom, I am never accepting his help.

788
00:46:07,380 --> 00:46:10,190
- Whatever it is, I will do it. - Your dad is worried about you.

789
00:46:11,860 --> 00:46:14,020
I heard you failed your interview this time too.

790
00:46:14,060 --> 00:46:16,560
Mom, it is too late. I am hanging up.

791
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:22,700
I have to take the TOEFL.

792
00:46:23,300 --> 00:46:25,140
I have to rewrite my cover letter too.

793
00:46:27,070 --> 00:46:29,240
Should I just quit everything and get a certification?

794
00:46:31,340 --> 00:46:32,540
Oh, whatever.

795
00:46:59,070 --> 00:47:00,170
I am hungry.

796
00:47:03,110 --> 00:47:04,910
(Welcome)

797
00:47:05,910 --> 00:47:08,850
- Hello. - Hey, student, you are here.

798
00:47:08,910 --> 00:47:11,010
Oh, I keep telling you I am not a student.

799
00:47:11,080 --> 00:47:13,550
- One spicy pork, please. - Got it, take a seat.

800
00:47:39,680 --> 00:47:41,040
- Eat up. - Thank you.

801
00:47:45,620 --> 00:47:47,850
What? Tak...

802
00:47:48,250 --> 00:47:49,820
Are you Tak Mu I?

803
00:47:50,790 --> 00:47:51,860
Hello.

804
00:47:52,420 --> 00:47:53,860
Oh, hi.

805
00:47:56,060 --> 00:47:58,700
Thanks to you, I enjoyed the lunchbox.

806
00:48:01,130 --> 00:48:03,070
Lunchbox?

807
00:48:03,400 --> 00:48:04,630
I have a question.

808
00:48:06,040 --> 00:48:07,440
How did you know?

809
00:48:07,940 --> 00:48:09,840
My house, my daily route.

810
00:48:11,740 --> 00:48:14,440
Do you happen to live in the same neighborhood as me?

811
00:48:16,810 --> 00:48:20,320
What? Oh, I do not know what you are talking about...

812
00:48:20,780 --> 00:48:23,290
You are the one who sent food to my house, right?

813
00:48:23,350 --> 00:48:24,520
Me?

814
00:48:24,850 --> 00:48:27,190
- Why would I do that? - How should I know?

815
00:48:27,390 --> 00:48:28,860
Probably because you are my fan.

816
00:48:29,230 --> 00:48:31,630
Oh, I am not your fan, Tak Mu I.

817
00:48:34,530 --> 00:48:35,530
I'm serious.

818
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:40,270
Then if you are not a fan, why are you following me to my sets?

819
00:48:40,700 --> 00:48:41,770
And the convenience store...

820
00:48:42,910 --> 00:48:45,310
Did you get a job there knowing I go there often?

821
00:48:49,680 --> 00:48:52,920
Right, whatever it is, I would like you to stop now.

822
00:48:53,980 --> 00:48:55,890
Oh, I keep telling you it is not me.

823
00:48:55,920 --> 00:48:58,260
Why do you keep making me out to be some weirdo?

824
00:48:58,320 --> 00:49:01,630
So meeting here is just a coincidence too?

825
00:49:01,690 --> 00:49:05,500
What else would it be, destiny? I am a regular here too.

826
00:49:13,470 --> 00:49:14,870
Eat this.

827
00:49:14,970 --> 00:49:16,670
As you saw, I have not even touched it.

828
00:49:20,880 --> 00:49:21,950
What is his deal?

829
00:49:43,900 --> 00:49:46,000
What is going on? Did the young man leave?

830
00:49:47,470 --> 00:49:48,640
Here, please put it over here.

831
00:49:52,480 --> 00:49:53,810
It is so good.

832
00:49:57,650 --> 00:50:02,520
My, even though she is skinny, she sure has a hearty appetite.

833
00:50:05,590 --> 00:50:06,690
Excuse me.

834
00:50:06,790 --> 00:50:09,430
What did the man who just left order?

835
00:50:09,560 --> 00:50:10,660
He had the spicy pork.

836
00:50:18,500 --> 00:50:20,000
("Rooftop Romance")

837
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:23,610
What? Hey.

838
00:50:24,110 --> 00:50:25,110
Over there...

839
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:27,910
Hey, stop.

840
00:50:29,680 --> 00:50:32,980
Stalker fan, this is a filming set. Please leave.

841
00:50:33,080 --> 00:50:34,780
I am just going home.

842
00:50:34,820 --> 00:50:36,420
Hey, come on.

843
00:50:36,820 --> 00:50:38,490
Could you please move out of the way?

844
00:50:38,560 --> 00:50:40,820
I have been working all day without a wink of sleep,

845
00:50:40,890 --> 00:50:42,960
so I really do not have the energy to argue.

846
00:50:43,030 --> 00:50:46,300
Then stop following us around and exhausting us both.

847
00:50:46,360 --> 00:50:48,230
Oh, my, a moth. Go away!

848
00:50:48,300 --> 00:50:51,200
What is it? Oh, my, what is this?

849
00:51:10,890 --> 00:51:11,890
Goodness!

850
00:51:16,260 --> 00:51:17,630
What?

851
00:51:36,380 --> 00:51:37,680
Hey, are you okay?

852
00:51:44,190 --> 00:51:46,220
What is your name?

853
00:51:46,690 --> 00:51:48,020
Gong Yu Il.

854
00:51:49,530 --> 00:51:51,030
"Holiday?"

855
00:51:51,260 --> 00:51:54,430
No, not holiday, Yu Il.

856
00:51:54,500 --> 00:51:55,530
As in "only one."

857
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:59,970
- Are you okay? - Do you think he is?

858
00:52:01,170 --> 00:52:02,670
I am sorry.

859
00:52:02,740 --> 00:52:04,110
Hey.

860
00:52:04,170 --> 00:52:06,380
Do you know what it feels like to have a moth fly into your mouth?

861
00:52:06,510 --> 00:52:07,510
I am sorry.

862
00:52:07,511 --> 00:52:11,510
It was flapping around and struggling to survive in there.

863
00:52:11,610 --> 00:52:15,420
Gosh, I could feel its legs and wings.

864
00:52:15,550 --> 00:52:18,390
And there is this powdery stuff coating my mouth and tongue.

865
00:52:18,460 --> 00:52:21,320
- Even if I brush, it feels gross. - Wait.

866
00:52:22,030 --> 00:52:23,960
If you need to go to the hospital,

867
00:52:23,990 --> 00:52:26,400
- I will pay your medical bills... - No.

868
00:52:26,460 --> 00:52:29,200
This was clearly an accident,

869
00:52:30,470 --> 00:52:32,070
so I will let it go.

870
00:52:32,100 --> 00:52:35,640
- Really? - But promise me one thing.

871
00:52:37,040 --> 00:52:38,510
What promise?

872
00:52:38,910 --> 00:52:41,540
Do not follow me around anymore.

873
00:52:42,910 --> 00:52:45,010
And no more food.

874
00:52:47,080 --> 00:52:48,380
Wait a minute.

875
00:52:49,050 --> 00:52:50,850
Let me be clear.

876
00:52:51,250 --> 00:52:53,060
That was not me.

877
00:52:53,320 --> 00:52:54,760
What do I have to do to make you believe me?

878
00:52:57,360 --> 00:52:58,760
Well...

879
00:52:58,800 --> 00:53:03,370
Do you not see this right here? I am a huge fan of Ryu Min.

880
00:53:04,770 --> 00:53:06,000
It really was not you?

881
00:53:06,040 --> 00:53:07,870
She must be a Revolving Door.

882
00:53:08,170 --> 00:53:11,540
- A Revolving Door? - You become a fan, spin, and leave.

883
00:53:11,610 --> 00:53:13,510
Join, leave, join, leave.

884
00:53:13,540 --> 00:53:15,780
People who switch favorites like it is nothing. Look here.

885
00:53:16,780 --> 00:53:18,780
Being a Revolving Door and stalking...

886
00:53:18,850 --> 00:53:20,120
That is not love!

887
00:53:21,720 --> 00:53:23,390
- Excuse me. - Yes.

888
00:53:23,490 --> 00:53:25,890
I am truly sorry about the moth.

889
00:53:25,990 --> 00:53:29,360
And I appreciate Tak Mu I being so understanding about it.

890
00:53:29,830 --> 00:53:31,130
However,

891
00:53:31,160 --> 00:53:34,530
both you and Tak Mu I remind me of something.

892
00:53:37,670 --> 00:53:39,470
Like an awful customer who speaks Japanese well,

893
00:53:39,540 --> 00:53:41,670
but cannot speak English.

894
00:53:44,470 --> 00:53:46,840
Wait, you mean me?

895
00:53:46,910 --> 00:53:49,910
- How so? - You keep stubbornly insisting.

896
00:53:50,010 --> 00:53:52,080
If you are going to be like this, go check the security cameras.

897
00:53:52,150 --> 00:53:54,350
- Stop falsely accusing me. - I did, but...

898
00:53:54,420 --> 00:53:55,950
- Hey. - Yes.

899
00:53:58,250 --> 00:53:59,290
Wait outside.

900
00:54:00,460 --> 00:54:01,460
Are you sure?

901
00:54:12,070 --> 00:54:13,370
If it was not you,

902
00:54:13,940 --> 00:54:15,040
I apologize.

903
00:54:24,650 --> 00:54:26,320
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 3)

904
00:54:27,720 --> 00:54:29,950
Oh, the door is this way...

905
00:54:30,020 --> 00:54:31,020
Wait...

906
00:54:34,320 --> 00:54:37,590
- Where did you get this? - Do not touch my things.

907
00:54:38,800 --> 00:54:40,030
Give it back, right now.

908
00:54:40,100 --> 00:54:41,259
If you tell me how an unpublished book...

909
00:54:41,260 --> 00:54:42,470
ended up here.

910
00:54:43,430 --> 00:54:45,740
Hurry up and give it to me. Give it back.

911
00:54:45,800 --> 00:54:48,770
Hand it over right now.
